       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is five times the usual maximum metformin dose of about 2,550 mg/day (850 mg TID). A single 4250 mg dose is also far above the normal per-dose range of 500\u20131000 mg. At this level there's a serious risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg** PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **425 mg** PO TID, if the dose was meant to be lower\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg** PO BID or TID\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 4250 mg really is intended, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
