     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Metformin at 12,750 mg/day has no therapeutic use. It's about five times the maximum dose, and it carries a high risk of severe lactic acidosis even with normal kidney and liver function. Confirming the dose didn't change that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower starting dose if the patient is new to metformin.\n- **Add a note to the order.** It could ask for pharmacy review or say that the dose was discussed with pharmacy.\n\nIf you think the order needs a dose above the labeled range, please take it through your pharmacy or attending and your hospital's override process. I'm not the right place for that decision.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
